    "description": "Move the cases pin to the D6 goldens and write the 0.5.0 baseline\n\nMoves `eval/cases.json` to jerridan/pr-review-cases@e6ddf81, which holds the 25 labeled findings of the D6 gate run as goldens (jerridan/pr-review-cases#5: 22 posted, 3 not real; the set now holds 82 goldens, 51 posted). Writes the new `eval/baseline.json` from one run of pr-review 0.5.0 on the ten cases, one repeat, `--no-extras`. Adds a Done line under D4b in TICKETS.md.\n\n| metric | old baseline (0.4.0, 29 posted goldens) | new baseline (0.5.0, 51 posted goldens) |\n|---|---|---|\n| recall | 0.287 | 0.396 |\n| precision | 0.636 | 0.722 |\n| cost per PR | $4.25 | $4.65 |\n| cases completed | 9 of 10 | 10 of 10 |\n\nRecall is over a larger denominator now, so it is not comparable with the 0.433 of PR #39 against the old set. Precision rises because the goldens now list what the verifier posts and the labeler confirmed.\n\nThe margins stay at recall 0.1 and precision 0.35. The README rule derives a margin from the spread of the repeats, and one repeat gives no spread, so the existing margins stand. Both remain at least 0.05 below their baseline values.\n\nPer case (recall, precision, posted, cost):\n\n```\nmartian-calcom-8330                 0.571  0.571  7  $8.43\nmartian-discourse-graphite-1        0.500  0.667  6  $10.83\nmartian-sentry-93824                0.778  0.875  8  $4.65\nmartian-sentry-greptile-1           0.778  0.875  8  $11.16\nreviewbench-axios-10836             0.500  1.000  1  $0.54\nreviewbench-claire-de-binare-1550   0.000  -      0  $2.71\nreviewbench-disaster-ninja-fe-1166  0.333  1.000  1  $2.01\nreviewbench-ensnode-1938            0.333  1.000  1  $2.07\nreviewbench-flatten-js-244          0.167  0.333  3  $1.43\nreviewbench-statswales-frontend-626 0.000  0.000  1  $2.64\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZfeb8Fxs7Pynw8RhjV\n",
